{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>ואהי</b> — a past-tense verb, regarding the evils that HaShem brought upon them." "<b>אשור</b> — an epithet, like עצום (mighty), that men's באשורי (footsteps) would go in it, and so forth. n: The phrase ועוד ('and so forth') gestures at further examples of this pattern; the syntax of the intermediate clause is compressed and the translation is hyper-literal."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:10.988678834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}